,title,link,text,language,family
0,Konyak languages - Wikipedia,https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Konyak_languages,"The Konyak languages, or alternatively the Konyakian, Northern Naga, or Patkaian languages, is a branch of Sino-Tibetan languages spoken by various Naga peoples in southeastern Arunachal Pradesh and northeastern Nagaland states of northeastern India.","Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
1,List of ethnic groups in Myanmar - Wikipedia,https://web.archive.org/web/20230314194838/https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/List_of_ethnic_groups_in_Myanmar,"Toggle List grouped by language family subsection. 2.1 Sino-Tibetan. 2.2 Tai–Kadai. 2.3 Hmong–Mien.Naga, Long Phuri [lpn]. Naga, Makuri [jmn].","Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
2,"Naga, Long Phuri Language (LPN)... | Ethnologue Free",https://www.ethnologue.com/language/lpn,Long Phuri Naga is a stable indigenous language of Myanmar. It belongs to the Sino-Tibetan language family.,"Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
3,Long Phuri language,https://grokipedia.com/page/long_phuri_language,"Long Phuri Naga (also known as Long Phuri or Amimi Naga) is a Sino-Tibetan language of the Naga branch spoken by approximately 2,200 people as a first language in six villages of Layshi Township, Hkamti District, Sagaing Region, northwestern Myanmar.","Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
4,"Naga, Long Phuri in Myanmar (Burma) people group... | Joshua Project",https://joshuaproject.net/index.php/people_groups/18963/BM,"Long Phuri Naga are also called Amimi Naga. Their language has traditionally been classified as a Makuri Naga dialect. However, it is clear that Long Phuri is a distinct language from Makuri. Historically, the Naga are the peoples who live in the Brahmaputra and Chindwin valleys.","Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
5,Sino-Tibetan,https://lingweb.eva.mpg.de/channumerals/Sino-Tibetan.htm,"The Sino-Tibetan Language Phylum. SiniticUnclassified: Darlong, Khamba, Koro, Akyaung Ari Naga, Inpui Naga, Jejara Naga, Kokak Naga, Long Phuri Naga, Makuri Naga, Puimei Naga, Ranglong.","Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
6,docs.verbix.com/Languages/Sino-Tibetan,https://docs.verbix.com/Languages/Sino-Tibetan,"The Sino-Tibetan languages form a hypothetical language family composed of, at least, the Chinese and the Tibeto-Burman languages, including some 400 languages of East Asia.[lpn] Long Phuri Naga. [jmn] Makuri Naga.","Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
7,Long Phuri Naga Literacy | Bibles International,https://biblesint.org/languages/long-phuri-naga-literacy,"The Long Phuri Naga people reside in the Layshi township in the Sagaing state of Myanmar. Numbering between 1,000 and 2,500, with an additional 4,500 living in neighboring countries, approximately 98% of the Long Phuri profess Christianity.","Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
8,OLAC resources in and about the Long Phuri Naga language,http://olac.ldc.upenn.edu/language/lpn,"ONLINENaga, Long Phuri: a language of Myanmar. n.a. 2018. SIL International. oai:ethnologue.com:lpn. Other known names and dialect names: Amimi Naga, Longpfuri, Longpfuru, Mimi, Long Phuri Naga.","Naga, Long Phuri",Sino-Tibetan
